    "math_academy_id": "q-162175",
    "knowledge_point_id": "1577f765-f98c-5020-8e45-8da2c5f092e6",
    "knowledge_point": "Determining the Area Scale Factor of an Affine Transformation",
    "problem": "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?",
    "worked_solution": "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|3|=3.\n$$",
